course: dictionary
lesson: 6214
title: Mist: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one to use. «Breathed-out air is warm and full of water vapour, which turns into tiny droplets of mist on cold glass.» Here mist means the tiny drops of water that cover the glass.
explain: Mist can also be a thin fog that makes it hard to see far. In safety, mist on roads or hills means you must slow down. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Mist can be a verb too, an action word. «A bathroom mirror mists up during a hot shower» means the mirror gets covered with tiny drops. Your eyes can mist as well, when tears come. The words around mist always give you the clue.
fact: Mist means lots of tiny drops of water in the air close to the ground, which makes it hard to see far.
fact: Mist forms when warm, damp air cools and water vapour turns into tiny droplets.
fact: Mist can also mean a fine spray of liquid, as in «a mist of rain».
fact: «Mist up» means to cover with tiny drops, as in «the mirror misted up».
fact: When your eyes mist, tears are coming, so the word can describe feelings as well as weather.
exercise: «Your breath shows up as mist on a cold window.» What does mist mean here? | A loud noise from the window | A bright light shining through the glass | A type of cold, hard ice | *Tiny drops of water on the glass
exercise: «When researchers sprayed a harmless mist into the trees, beetles fell out.» What does mist mean here? | *A fine spray of liquid | A thick, dark cloud of smoke | A cold wind blowing hard | A sudden flash of light
exercise: In safety, mist on the hills makes it hard to see. What should walkers and drivers do? | Run faster to get home | Stop reading the map | Turn their lights off | *Slow down
test: «A bathroom mirror mists up during a hot shower.» What does mists mean here? | Is wiped clean with a cloth | Shines very brightly | Breaks into small pieces | *Gets covered with tiny drops
test: «Her eyes misted as she said goodbye.» What does misted mean here? | She closed her eyes to sleep | *Tears came into her eyes | She began to laugh loudly | She could not see because it was dark
exam: Which meaning of mist fits «a morning mist hung over the valley», and how can you check it? | A tear, so check that the valley is sad | A fine spray of liquid, so check the valley is wet | *Thin fog close to the ground, so check it still makes sense | To cover with drops, so check the mist moves
